   "explain": "\\( 8 - 3 = 5 \\)."
  }
 ],
 "intro": "Counting elements of a union needs one extra step: do not count the overlap twice.",
 "takeaways": [
  "n(A) = only A + both",
  "n(A ∪ B) = n(A) + n(B) − n(A ∩ B)"
 ],
 "notes": [
  {
   "title": "When A and B do not overlap",
   "text": "If nothing is in both, n(A ∩ B) = 0 and the formula is just n(A) + n(B)."
  }
 ],
